{"schema_version":"appworld-codex-plan-v1","status":"candidate","failure_reason":"","missing_public_schema_fields":[],"task_id":"82e2fac_1","task_family":"82e2fac","completion_mode":"answer_variable","plan_summary":"Inspect the required public APIs, authenticate to Spotify with supervisor-provided credentials, exhaustively paginate the playlist library, fetch every distinct referenced song, derive the uniquely highest-liked title, and submit that answer.","steps":[{"step_index":1,"phase":"inspect","reasoning":"The public documentation for every required API must be inspected before making the first task API call.","action_code":"public_api_docs = {\n    \"supervisor.show_profile\": apis.supervisor.show_profile.__doc__,\n    \"supervisor.show_account_passwords\": apis.supervisor.show_account_passwords.__doc__,\n    \"spotify.login\": apis.spotify.login.__doc__,\n    \"spotify.show_playlist_library\": apis.spotify.show_playlist_library.__doc__,\n    \"spotify.show_song\": apis.spotify.show_song.__doc__,\n    \"supervisor.complete_task\": apis.supervisor.complete_task.__doc__,\n}\nprint(public_api_docs)","depends_on_steps":[],"api_names_used":["supervisor.show_profile","supervisor.show_account_passwords","spotify.login","spotify.show_playlist_library","spotify.show_song","supervisor.complete_task"],"mutates_state":false,"verification_targets":["Required public API documentation is available for review before task calls."],"output_policy":"public_records"},{"step_index":2,"phase":"authenticate","reasoning":"The supervisor profile supplies the Spotify username, while the password must be selected from the supervisor's account-password records without exposing it.","action_code":"supervisor_profile = apis.supervisor.show_profile()\naccount_password_records = apis.supervisor.show_account_passwords()\nspotify_password_records = [record for record in account_password_records if record[\"account_name\"].strip().lower() == \"spotify\"]\nif len(spotify_password_records) != 1:\n    raise ValueError(\"Expected exactly one Spotify password record\")\nspotify_username = supervisor_profile[\"email\"]\nspotify_password = spotify_password_records[0][\"password\"]\nspotify_login_result = apis.spotify.login(username=spotify_username, password=spotify_password)\nspotify_access_token = spotify_login_result[\"access_token\"]\nprint({\"spotify_password_record_count\": len(spotify_password_records), \"token_type\": spotify_login_result[\"token_type\"]})","depends_on_steps":[1],"api_names_used":["supervisor.show_profile","supervisor.show_account_passwords","spotify.login"],"mutates_state":false,"verification_targets":["Exactly one Spotify credential record is selected.","A Spotify access token is stored without printing credentials or the token."],"output_policy":"safe_aggregate"},{"step_index":3,"phase":"observe","reasoning":"All playlists in the authenticated user's library must be collected across pagination before determining which songs are in scope.","action_code":"first_playlist_page = apis.spotify.show_playlist_library(access_token=spotify_access_token)\nplaylist_pages = [first_playlist_page]\npage_index = 1\nwhile True:\n    playlist_page = apis.spotify.show_playlist_library(access_token=spotify_access_token, page_index=page_index)\n    playlist_pages.append(playlist_page)\n    if not playlist_page:\n        break\n    page_index += 1\nplaylist_by_id = {}\nfor playlist_page in playlist_pages:\n    for playlist in playlist_page:\n        playlist_by_id[playlist[\"playlist_id\"]] = playlist\nplaylists = list(playlist_by_id.values())\nplaylist_song_references = [song_id for playlist in playlists for song_id in playlist[\"song_ids\"]]\nunique_song_ids = list(dict.fromkeys(playlist_song_references))\nprint({\"playlist_count\": len(playlists), \"song_reference_count\": len(playlist_song_references), \"unique_song_count\": len(unique_song_ids), \"pages_requested_including_terminal_page\": len(playlist_pages)})","depends_on_steps":[2],"api_names_used":["spotify.show_playlist_library"],"mutates_state":false,"verification_targets":["Playlist pages are requested through the terminal empty page.","Song IDs are derived only from returned playlist records.","Duplicate playlist and song references are normalized."],"output_policy":"safe_aggregate"},{"step_index":4,"phase":"observe","reasoning":"The like count and title needed for comparison are available only from each referenced song's public detail record.","action_code":"song_details_by_id = {}\nfor song_id in unique_song_ids:\n    song_record = apis.spotify.show_song(song_id=song_id)\n    song_details_by_id[song_record[\"song_id\"]] = song_record\nsong_records = list(song_details_by_id.values())\nprint({\"requested_unique_song_count\": len(unique_song_ids), \"retrieved_unique_song_count\": len(song_records)})","depends_on_steps":[3],"api_names_used":["spotify.show_song"],"mutates_state":false,"verification_targets":["A song detail record is retrieved for every distinct song ID found in the playlists."],"output_policy":"safe_aggregate"},{"step_index":5,"phase":"derive","reasoning":"With all in-scope song records available, the answer can be derived by comparing their returned like counts and reviewing whether the resulting title is unambiguous.","action_code":"if not song_records:\n    raise ValueError(\"No songs were found in the Spotify playlists\")\nmaximum_like_count = max(song[\"like_count\"] for song in song_records)\nmost_liked_song_candidates = [song for song in song_records if song[\"like_count\"] == maximum_like_count]\ncandidate_titles = sorted({song[\"title\"] for song in most_liked_song_candidates})\nif len(candidate_titles) != 1:\n    raise ValueError(\"The most-liked title is ambiguous\")\nanswer_title = candidate_titles[0]\nprint({\"most_liked_candidates\": [{\"song_id\": song[\"song_id\"], \"title\": song[\"title\"], \"like_count\": song[\"like_count\"]} for song in most_liked_song_candidates]})","depends_on_steps":[4],"api_names_used":[],"mutates_state":false,"verification_targets":["The maximum is computed across every retrieved in-scope song.","All songs tied at the maximum are reviewed.","The answer title is unambiguous before submission."],"output_policy":"public_records"},{"step_index":6,"phase":"complete","reasoning":"The answer variable has been derived exclusively from the exhaustively retrieved playlist and song records and is ready for QA-task submission.","action_code":"completion_result = apis.supervisor.complete_task(answer=answer_title)","depends_on_steps":[5],"api_names_used":["supervisor.complete_task"],"mutates_state":true,"verification_targets":["The derived song title is submitted as the task answer."],"output_policy":"no_print"}]}